 "notes": "Curve extracted from the vector paths of PlotA.pdf (Fig. 'Constraints and projected reach for ALP-neutron couplings', fig:gannbounds). Reported curve is the lower envelope (union) of the three shaded blue 95% C.L. exclusion regions labeled 'This work [I]/[II]/[III]' (datasets: Vasilakis thesis, Kornack thesis, Brown thesis K-3He comagnetometers). The paper plots g_aNN in GeV^-1 defined via L = -g_aNN dmu(a) Nbar g5 gmu N; converted to canonical dimensionless g_an = 2 m_n g_aNN with m_n = 0.93957 GeV. Axes calibrated from PDF tick marks (x: 10^-24..10^-3 eV; y: 10^-13..10^-2 GeV^-1). Dataset III bound continues below the plotted range to arbitrarily small masses; points start at the plot's left edge 1e-24 eV, with the plateau g_aNN ~ 2.0e-7 GeV^-1 (from the 143-day constant-field bound) for m_a < 1.8e-22 eV. Highly jagged sections were mildly median-filtered (~0.05 dex) and sampled at ~0.075 dex, so narrow spikes are smoothed. Assumes ALPs are all of local DM, rho = 0.4 GeV/cm^3, mean velocity 232 km/s; stochastic-field corrections included by the authors. Electron-coupling bound (Fig. gaeebounds) also derived but neutron coupling is the headline result.",
